Kindergarten school is also part of the offices have included the architects.
Avriopoint de Brno is the new head office of the company Arch.
No one could have expected it to also house a mini-kindergarten school with everything you need - colorful walls, imaginative furniture, toys and finally a miniature playground on the terrace.
Since October of the last year, the children of the employees of Arch. design can be visited.
architectitonic project company, whose workshops have produced a large number of buildings in Brno, has ensued its mini-mursing company since the first sketches of the Avriopoint building.
It employs about 90 people, especially of their age, and it was important for women architects and project managers to return to work quickly.
At the same time as reduced-time employment contracts, the nursery school is a bonus offered to its employees by the company Arch. Design as part of its social program.
Builders and  architects thus have the opportunity to combine work that takes care for children.
It was the employees of Arch.Designeux themselves who imagined this nursery school and with the support of the management they were able to obtain an allocation from the European Union and the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs.
Mini-Supreserve School is funded from the European Social Fund through the Operational Human Resources Programme and the State Budget of the Czech Republic.
As a result of the financing endowments (2.28 million Czech koruna), they were able to purchase equipment and appliances and after two years provide qualified personnel and start-up.
After the use of the funding endowment (two-year), the company Arch. Design has an obligation after 3 years to operate the mini nursery school from its own funds.
The preparation of the project lasted one year and it was the company Economy rating that helped to make an application for endowment.
Child care was provided by a trained staff, all day a nurse and a kindergarten teacher took care of the children; children could go to nursery school without an age limit, but most of them were more than three years old.
Since it is a "mini nursery school", there can be only 5 children present at the same time, but over the course of the day there are more to replace each other.
The functioning of the school was flexible according to the needs of the parents and the children of all employees had the same right to use this school without regard to the hierarchical position.
Although individual care and education, the curriculum of the mini-currency school is comparable to that for pre-school education.
Children do not only play, but quality education is also ensured - from the very beginning to the school benches is taught.
The class is equipped not only with imaginative to toys and games but also with a computer that children can use.
The presence of small children in society creates a friendly and positive environment.
Persecutors can at any time check their child and do not have the stress of delay in picking up the children from a school away from the parents' place of work.
Parents therefore use their working time in the most productive way.
It is no wonder that a natural relationship of loyalty is created between the employee and the employer.
Arch.Designs is thus listed among companies that offer a bonus of choice for the recruitment of new employees and that are friendly to the family and through this program strengthens HR marketing.
The bone house still fascinates after 100 years. Take a look in Gaudi's interiors.
The roof resembles the back of a prehistoric Saurian, the stair staircase to a dinosaur spine, and balconies with open fish mouths.
The Casa Battlo house in Barcelona by the architect Antoni Gaudi.
Due to its organic shapes, the house was nicknamed Bone from the local.
Organic forms, wild colors, unusual use of stones, fragments of tiles and mosaic, facade reminiscent of flakes and everywhere present of the curves, that's all that is typical for Antoni Gaudi 'Art Nouveau.
The frontal facade of the house unrolls its dream lines, pleasant colors and textures reminiscent of nature and animals.
During a more detailed observation, the geometry, the rhythm and the order designed with precision.
In the night the facade of the house becomes even more dramatic and is lit in such a way that the impression of brilliance of the colors is reinforced.
The winding and twisting of the shapes also appears in the indoors with the same measurement.
Wash-copies window frames, balustrades, decorative elements of doors, eilleton and lamella.
The Battlo house which rises in the Eixample district in the merchant street Passeig de Gracia at number 43, was born from the construction of an 1877 house by the architect Emilio Sala Cortes.
Reconstruction took place for two years and the house was completed in 1906.
Investor Joseph Battlo, a wealthy entrepreneur, initially insisted on demolishing the old-fashioned construction and the construction of another brand-new but quickly accepted Gaudi’s idea of an unparalleled and cheaper reconstruction.
But Casa Battlo's idea as a multi-family house was not conceived by Gaudi alone.
Architect Josep Maria Jujol worked with him.
Precisely on his project came the de decorations for an apartment representing the owner of the building and the use of mosaic for facade.
The facade also worked on other artists and creators.
The joint work of the Casa Battlo factory began with successful cooperation between Jujol and Gaudi.
Jujol participated in the construction of Gaudi Casa Mila's house and Guell park where there are other works by Gaudi.
The premises nicknamed the hot house just after it was finished because of its organic "House of Bone" forms.
Others, with regard to the specific mechanism for opening the windows, have called it "the sifting house".
It is said that at the top of the construction there is a sword similar to that of Saint George the patron of Catalonia.
Other building sculpture elements contain hidden religious patterns.
Gaudi conceived for the house a unique system of central heavier, with typical ventilation vents and chimneys.
Their 45-degree inclination seems weird.
In the course of Gaudi did not strictly comply with the construction guidelines at that time and did not allow itself to be hindered by them.
At the beginning of the construction he obtained from the city the building permit, knowing, of course, that the data on the reconstruction plans was so vague that two years later during the completion the municipal council was horrified and asked for changes.
For example, the members of the municipal council did not like the pillars of the construction encroach on the public sidewalk.
There was never a change, but, on the other hand, only 15 days after Josep Battlo called (and got satisfaction) permission to rent the two highest floors.
The landlord moved to the lower floors.
In the gallery on the second floor there was a shared loun loun lounge and in the third bed bed bedroom and a private part of the apartment.
The ground floor was rented to a jewellery store.
The entire six-storey house is shared by a staircase through which one accesses to an independent roof terrace.
All the right angles and straight lines were cancelled by the basic elements of the reconstruction and their replacement by curvature walls.
Gaudi also travailed the modern concept of connecting spaces.
The common part can be completely connected by opening lounge gates, and high-society can communicate comfortably or limit the private space for more intimate maintenance.
The house with Gaudi's reconstruction received new facial faculties a non-requirsite and additional two-storey roof.
Gaudi's game with the light is also animating, blue and white glazed ziles with which the inner yard is decorated and with pactive shafts.
The two-color game gives a maximum of light in all floors of the house.
Simply thrill on the principle that the white reflects more than the dark, which on the other hand absorbs the rays of the sun.
The Casa Battlo house which was included in the UNESCO World Heritage Fund in 2005 can be visited by everyone.
On the first floor of the house is the most spacious and splendid apartment accessible to the public.
Owners decided to take this step in 2002 on the 150th Anniversary Anniversary Anniversary of Famous Creator.
They continued the visits because they noted that it was a lucrative business and they extended the scope of visits to common areas and attractive stores, including roof terraces.
Entrance ticket to the monument is really inexpensive and costs EUR 16.50; students, retirees, groups and tourist card holders have 20 per cent rebate.
The sum is still above the entry price into Gaudi's other buildings in the city.
If you want to feel the real atmosphere of the house with its fantastic turrets, you must quickly find a comrade among the inhabitants of the building and completely visit the house.
