However, the troops of the Rapid Intervention Squad have recently complained to Minister Vondra that they have virtually no ammunition for their handguns and that firing sessions are limited due to the need for money.
About the lack of body laundry we don't talk about it.
'And I don't take my head if they buy such a large quantity of detonating ropes from us.'
"And it's their decision and they really know what they're doing."
