The Ministry of Defence now has major problems in neutralising dozens of tons of ammunition from the time of the Warsaw Co- Pact, when the Czechoslovakia army of two hundred thrivers was preparing to move, heading on the Rhine.
What the Czech army awaits in a few years' time that MF DNES has contacted: neutralising hundreds of kilometres of deceitful old-fashioned ropes that it is now buying 'cheap'.
Up to now I benefit from the contacts that I have obtained through the competitions.
The franchise sale of his hotel helped Lukas Pytloun well for the win-in-writing of the Best Individual Entrepreneur Contest.
The winner of the Best Individual Entrepreneur contest last year was Lukas Pytloun, a 28-year-old entrepreneur.
His adventure towards success is like in a film.
Lukas Pytloun liked to travel.
And abroad, he realized that in Libérec lacked a quality hosting site at a reasonable price.
Of his savings on what he had earned while working abroad and with the help of a bank loan, he bought a small building with five half-broken apartments.
Knowing that he was still a student in the third year of graduating from higher education, it was a courageous action.
'The relationship between the quality and the price of accommodation in our region made me want to do something,' says Lucas Pytloun.
He started renting the first rebuilt apartment to foreign workers.
He reinvested the profit in the building which he transformed into a board with 54 beds.
From then on, its work as an entrepreneur has enabled it to open four boarding houses, two style-style restaurants and two hotels with a total capacity of nearly 300 beds of all categories of accommodation.
The most comfortable among them was until very recently the four-star Pytloun design hotel.
This year it has come up with another of the same quality.
"We have just signed a contract with a hotel in Ostrova Ostrova U Tise where we sold our franchise concept and other candidates for the Pytloun hotel franchise came forward," the number one entrepreneurs last year.
'And for the sale of the licence to run a large-scale hotel the victory in Entreprecater of the Year Contest served well well, adds Pytloun with recognizability.
Victory gave him more popularity and was known in Libérec and its surroundings.
'People recognized me in the streets, congratulated me very often and, I have to say, it was very pleasant,' he recalls.
The Committee recommends participation in this competition to all those who are trying to do something.
It doesn't have to win, but any opportunity to be visible is good.
He says he uses his contacts and acquaintances until today that he could not have obtained in any other way.
'While those I've met through the contest I've started to maintain regular business relationships.
In his view, the fame related to success also had an impact on employees.
And it's about 70.
'I see in them especially the loyalty and the pride of engaging in something that has in general been recognised.'
'It is not by far the sole result of my personal work, but the result of a good job for all of us together.
'Only my name is pushed forward,' said Lucas Pytloun with modesty.
I wish my successor for a better year than we had in Farmet.
The euphoria of victory was vehilatedly replaced by the effects of the crisis.
Thanks to the sense of goal of the winner Farmet has the worst moments behind him.
Anyone who came to fetch the prize from Slovansky dum for first place in the Operem of the Year competition organised by Vodaphone last year is Karel Odarsky, the owner of the company Farmet.
The jury rewarded the efforts with which it transformed a tooling workshop at Ceska Skalice into a kroner-revenged 100-degrEY company.
'I can say that the reward not only encouraged me my collaborators and increased our self-confidence to combat the competition,' says the winner of last year's contest today.
At the beginning of the history of the company Farmet there was a desire to do something useful.
And thus, when the state proposed to Karel Odrasky to rent the small workshop as compensation after the confiscation of the property by the communists, it did not hesitate for a long time, refused a quarry in a company where he was working at the time, and created a company with some comrades in his father's surroundings for the manufacture of plastic buckets.
It wasn't very long after they started specializing in Vegetative Oil presses.
After eighteen years, it has become the largest manufacturer of Automotive Press in Central Europe.
The company was known even in the non-specialized audience after the success of the competition obtained through the media.
'Not only have our customers started to really get to know the Farmet brand but also the foreign partners who began to realize that they were collaborating with a company that obtained the greatest success in its country of origin,' says Karel zdarsky.
But the past year didn't go to Farmet only in the euphoria of the victory.
The evaluation of the company was based on the economic performance of 2008 and in part from 2009.
Precisely in 2009 it was the most difficult year for the sale of engineering machines.
At the height of the crisis, which did not really affect the citizens, the companies were forced to halt their investment projects and begin to limit their purchases of new materials and technologies.
'Obviously we have not escaped this situation.
'Revenues fell by 40 per cent, and we had to limit our production and even lay off,' explains Karel zdarsky.
A viable society must know that unpopular steps must be taken from time to time.
But they handled the situation properly and retained beneficial results, even though they were inferior to those before the pre-circacy.
In Farmet, however, they continued uncompromisingly investing in research and development.
'We've built with the endowments a training and research center, reinforced the company's presentation in international exhibition venues, and won the main awards in national exhibitions,' zdarsky says.
Everything leads us to believe that the crisis is behind them.
Gaming figures go back and with them the number of employees as well.
'To the new victor I wish this pleasant feeling of victory but in a quiet atmosphere,' says Karel Adarsky.
An investigation that removes insecure regulations.
For the fourth time, the Absurdity Inquiry of the Year was part of the business clan.
Some absurd regulations could have been removed.
