The effort to suppress absurd deeds is not a slice in the water.
In 2007, what didn't please people was an obligation for contractors to report three days to the office for the sole-companied business where the business is located, the intention to go to an exhibition or pilgrimage with a booth.
This obligation was abolished with the implementation of the Individual Enterprise Act.
The second most appropriated obligation in 2007, which was to declare to the Labour Office a 30-Daily Foreign Employee, has been discontinued with the so-called Green Card Act.
And everything is ok until the third session of the Contest.
The Absurdity of the Year 2009 was the decree for physiotherapists to have a large mirror in their practice, a refrigerator and two automatic weighing scales.
This has been changed by order of the Ministry of Health last year - the requirement to have a refrigerator has been removed.
A new category rewards socially responsible firms.
