At the Lands Fund in Plzen, the police carried out arrests during an open competition
The Anti-Corruption Publicity Fund building in Plzen has carried out arrests in recent days in recent days.
Defensives handcuffed Lubos and real-est real-store entrepreneur Lubo.
It had endeavoured precisely to manipulate a public call for tenders for the settlement of an application for restitution in such a way that the land proposed would be obtained by a particular candidate.
He owed Lubos G. half a million kroons.
"For the time being, I can only confirm that the police are suing an initiating person in the context of a public invitation to tender and competition," said the head of Plzen's Plzen Public Prosecutor's Office, knowing that it is forbidden to provide more explanation because the investigation is under way.
After 24 hours, the 46-year-at-writing stratigator were handed over.
To find out how it could influence an open competition, one can only speculate in the light of so little official information.
On a question from Pravo, the spokeswowoman of the Lubomira Cerna Land Fund stated that the police had actually made an arrest in Plzen at a separate workplace during the public competition.
'It has been a customer and by no means an employee,' she said.
The public competition according to Cerna has as its real name "Call to propose rights for the transfer of land according to the Land Law" and is put in place when there are a number of right-beared candidates.
'These individuals propose, as part of the appeal, a greater value of their rights to resitutions which must be settled before the value of the land is advertised.
'Depending on the proposed rights a ranking of the purchasers is set up and the Land Fund then transfers the land to the person who has proposed the highest rights,' explained the Fund's spokesman.
Lubos G. was clearly aware of the information concerning the persons who had subscribed to the appeal and, as it is himself, also a beneficiary because he had bought a large number of restitution rights, he had proposed to the candidates on the ground not to participate in the competition.
And it probably took care of the fact of retiring.
Which would explain why he had so much money in his possession at the time of his arrest.
