For example, the investigation of this case has been dragging on since June 2008 without a successful conclusion and "an increasing transformation into a serious problem of the credibility of the Agency", as recognized by a high-level Western diplomat serving at IAEA headquarters in Vienna, this is ultimately a serious violation of the nuclear-weapon-ban treaty.
The IAEA believes that in order to make progress, it is necessary to clarify the existence of the other three facilities, which must have a "functional relationship" with the alleged reactor.
So far, the inspectors have neither indicated what facilities they are dealing here, nor what their function or what they are suspected to contain.
