Nearly 250,000 Identity Cards, required for voting, were not yet distributed shortly prior to the election.
What is at stake is important.
Donors see the election of a popular and legitimate government as an important step in the reconstruction of Haiti.
It's so clear, Haitians do it themselves.
Pointing your feet towards the centre
The weeks after suddenly becoming a Widfamother, Argentina’s president Cristina Fernandez, benefited from a wave of public sympathy that has improved its approval rate by more than 50 per cent; this is its highest level since it was elected in 2007.
However, turning this into a successful campaign for a second term in an election next year could depend on Ms. Fernandez’s choice, which is visibly mourning, according to whether or not to abandon the intransigence of her late husband, predecessor and former political partner, Néstor Kirchner.
