Taiwan voters are moving towards a kind of closer union with the mainland.
What does Taiwan think of its older brother on the other side of the strait?
More than 7.5 million electors appeared on November 27, or 70 per cent of those eligible, to elect mayors and municipal councillors in five urban districts, as part of what is considered an overall assessment by President Ma Ying-jeou.
Mr. Ma himself became a substitute for feelings in relation to the Continent, having forged innovative business links, including a pact of partial free trade, in the greatest reorder of relations with China proper since 1949.
