Without policy, without opposition, without separation of powers, he said, corruption is inevitable.
According to India, the costs of corruption would amount to more than USD 300 billion a year on an all-year scale of corruption at a rate of more than USD 300 billion.
The non-governmental organization Transparency International was ranked 154th in a recent survey on the overall perception of corruption by the non-governmental organization Transparency International (the countries are ranked at least to the most corrupt).
