14 Supposed Drug Smugglers
About a dozen raids were carried out in Estrie on Wednesday as part of the dismantling of a network for the production and sale of cannabis.
Fourteen people have been arrested and will face various charges.
Searches took place in Sherbrooke, Orford and Stoke, the majority in places allegedly used for drug production.
'About 750 cannabis plants, four kilograms of hashish, money and equipment used for production were seized,' said Louis-Philippe Ruel, spokesman of the Sûreté du Québec.
Altogether, eleven men and three women were arrested, including the two alleged leaders of this network, two men from Sherbrooke.
Arriled persons had to appear at the Sherbrooke Judicial Palace within hours of their arrest.
They could deal with accusations of production of cannabis, possessation with the aim of trafficking, conspiracies and the theft of services, among others.
These searches took place as a result of a lengthy investigation, which lasted nearly a year.
'It's information received from the public that allowed us to make these arrests,' said Mr Ruel.
Some 70 police officers from the Regional Investigation Module de l'Estrie de la Sûreté du Quebec, the Sherbrooke Police Service and the Régie de Police Memphrémagog took part in this police operation.
